4. Powers and functions of the University: The University shall have the followingpowers and functions, namely. -
a) to providd for instructions in such branches of learning as it may deem fit, andto makq provisions for teaching, training, research and development oftechnologies and for the advancement and dissemination of knowledge in suchother fields/branches of study as the Board of Governors may determine;b) to make provisions for research and other services for the advancement anddissemination of knowledge in such a manner as it may determinec) to select, admit, teach, and examine students;d) to hold examinations and confer on or award degrees, diplomas, certificates,and other academic distinctions to and on persons who have passed itsexaminions under prescribed conditions;e) to confer honorary degrees and distinctions on approved persons in the mannerprescribed;f) to prescribe courses of studies in health, sciences, technologies and such otherbranches of learning as the University may determine;g) to institu-te programs for the exchange of students and teachers between theUniversity and Higher Education lnstitutes inside as well as outside Pakistan;h) to entef into agreements, contracts and arrangements with universities,organizations, institutions, bodies, and individuals for the purpose of carryingout functions and activities in Pakistan or abroad;i) to establish Faculties, Teaching Departments, Campuses, Colleges' lnstitutes,Museums, and other centers of learning for the development of teaching andresearch and to make such arrangements for their maintenance andmanagerient and administration as it may prescribe;j) to institute Professorship, Associate Professorship' Assistant Professorship,Lectureship, and any other posts and to appoint person thereto;k) to provide and support the academics developments of the faculty of theUniversity;l) to decide teaching methods and strategies to ensure the most effectlveeducational and training programs;m) to create'posts for teaching, research, administration, and other relatedfunctionS"and to appoint persons thereto;n) to receive and manage property transfened and grants, b€quests, trusts, gifts,donations, endowment, and other contributions made to it' and invest any fundsrepresenting such property, grants, bequests, trusts, gifts, donations,endowments, or contributions. To convert one kind of property into another, insuch a manner as it may deem fit;o) to institute and award fellowships, scholarships, exhibitions, bursaries, medals,and prizes under prescribed conditions;p) to develol and implement fund raising plans;q) to demand and receive fees and other charges as it may determine;r) to appoint members of various bodies and committees, as the Board maydetermine, for academic, administrative, and co-curricular activities;
