s) to appoint such officers and members of the staff as necessary and prescribe- terms and conditions and powers and duties of such offiGers and staff;t) to establish and support teaching hospitals;u) to supervise and control the discipline of the students of the university and topromote extra-curricular and recreational activities of students and to makearrangements for promoting their health;vy to provide career counselling and job search services to its studerits and alumni;w) to maintain linkages with alumni; andx) to do all srich other acts and things as may be requisite to further the objectivesof the Uniyersity as a place of education, learning and research;
5. Jurisdiction: The principal seat of the University shall be at lslamabad, and it mayset up any number oi campuses, col6ges, and institutes at such places in Pakistan asmay determine by the Board of Govemors subject to prior approval of the HigherEducation Commission (HEC).6' University open to all Glas36s, creeds, etc.: The University shall be open to allpersons of either glnder and of whatever religion, race, creed, class, colour or domicileand no person shall be denied the privileges of the university on the grounds of religion'race, caste, creed, class, colour or domicile.7. Teaching and Examinations of the university: (1) All recognized teaching,orofessional and technical training in various courses shall be conducted by the Universityor its constituent iblleges/units in the presciibed manner and may include lectures,tutorials, discussionS, Seminars, demonstrations, trainings, distance learning and othermethods of instruction as well as practical work in the laboratories, hospitals, workshopsand other governmental or private organizations subject to policies prescribed by theCommission.(2) The authority responsible for organizing recogniz€d teaching shall be such as may beprescribed..((3)TheUniversitymayassociateextemalexaminersfortheconductofexamlnationsorother duties as may be Prescribed.(4)TheUniversitymayprescribesyllabi,coursesofstudiesandinstructionsfortheconduct of studies and shall abide by the directions given by the Higher Educationcommission of Pakistan / Pakistan Medical & Dental council and other AccreditationCouncils.t(5) A degree shall not be awarded to a student unless he/she has passed an examinationin lslamic studies and Pakistan studies at the bachelor's degree level or in case of a Non-Muslim student in Ethics and Pakistan Studies at his/her option.
