CHAPTER IIIOFFICERS OF THE INSTITUTE
8. Officers of the University: - The following shall be the officers of the University,namely: -a. The Patrsn;b. The Chancellor;c. The Vice Chancellor;d. The Pro Vice Chancellor(s)e. The Deans;f. The Chairperson of the Teaching Oepartments:g. The Direetors of the Campusevcolleges/lnstitutes;h. The Prinqipal of the Constituent Unit;i. The Registrar;j. The Treasurer;k. The Controller.of Examinations;l. The Director Quality Enhancement Cell;m. The Resident Auditor; andn. Such other persons as may be prescribed by the Statutes, Regulations or Rulesto be the officers of the University.
9. The Patron: - (1 ) The President of the lslamic Republic of Pakistan shall be the Patronof the University.
(2)The Pakon shall, when present, preside al the Convocation of the University. ln theabsence ofthe Patrgn, the Chancellor shall preside overthe Convocation ofthe University.
(3)Every proposal tt confer an honorary degree shall be subject to confirmation by thePatron.
10. Visitation. - (1) The Patron may, in accordance with the terms and procedures asmay be prescribed, cause an inspection or inquiry lo be made on his own motion or at therequest of the commission in respect of any matter connected with the affairs of theUniversity and shall', from time to time, direct any person or persons to inquire into or carryout inspection of- ."r
(a) the University, its building, laboratories, libraries, and other facilities;(b) any institution, department or hospital maintained by the University;(c) the adequacy of financial and human resources;(d) the teaching, research, curiculum, examination, and other matters of the University;and(e) such other matters as the Patron may specify.
(2) The Pakon shall communicate to the Board of Governors his views with regard to theresult of visitation and shall, after ascertaining the views of the Board, advice the Boardon the action to be taken by it.
