(3) The Board shall,i{vithin such time as may be specified by the Chancellor, communicateto him such action, if any, as has been taken or may be proposed to be taken upon theresults of visitation. .
(4) Where the Board does not, within the time specified, take action to the satisfaction ofthe Patron, the Patron may issue such directions as he deems fit and the Board shallcomply with such diqections.
1'1. The Chancellbr: - (1) The Chancellor of the University, who shall preferably aperson of eminent in letters, sciences, or social work to be appointed by the Foundationon such terms and idnditions as may be prescribed.
(2)The Chancellor shall be the Chairperson of the Board of Governors.
(3)The Chancellor shall supervise the overall functioning of the University.'\(4)The members of the Board of Govemors as well as the Vice Chancellor shall beappointed by the Chahcellor.
(S)lf the Chancellor is satisfied that the proceedings of any Authority or orders of anyofficers are not in accordance with the provisions of this Ac1, the Statutes, the Regulations,or the Rules, he may after calling upon such Authority or officer to show cause in writing,appoint a five-memt er Review Panel to examine and report to the Chancellor' TheReview Panel shall be drawn from persons of eminence in academics and in the fields oflaw, accountancy andadministration.
(6)The Chancellor may subject to the provisions of this Act in his discretion, delegate allor any of the powers and functions of any Authority, officer, or employee of the universrtyto any authority, offiidr, or employe-e.rE(7)Should the chancellor be incapacitated from acting as such due to absence or anyother cause, the Vice -Chancellor shall act for him.
12. Removal from the Board of Governors. - (1) The chancellor may, upon therecommendation of the Review Panel, remove any person from the membership of theBoard of Governors gn the ground that such person:ai. has become of unsound mind; orii. has become incapacitated to function as member of the Board of Govemors; oriii. has been convict-ed by a court of law for an offence involving moral turpitude; oriv. has absented hlmself from three consecutive meetings without just cause; orv. has been guilty of misconduct, including use of position for personal advantage ofany kind, or grqFs inefficiency in the performance of functions.(2) The Chancellor ihall place the recommendations of Review Panel before the Board
