that: -
(a) the Deanihall hold office for three years and eligible for re- appointment'(b) the Deanthall present candidates for admission to degrees, (except honorarydegree) in the courses falling within the purview of the faculty; and(c) the Dean shall exercise such other powers and perform other duties as may beprescribed.
18. Registrar: (1) There shall be a Regislrar ofthe university to be appointed by the Boardof Governors on the i6commendation of the Selection Board,on such terms and conditions asmay be prescribed. *
(2)The experience a$ well as the professional and academic qualifications necessary forappointment to the post ofthe Registrar shall be as may be prescribed.(3)The Registrar shall be a full-time officer of the University and shall, -
be the admiqistrative head of the secretariat of the university and be responsiblefor the provision of secretariat support to the Authorities of the University;be the custodian of the common seal and the academic records of the University;maintain a register of registered graduates in the prescribed manner;
supervise the process of election, appointment, or nomination of members to thevarious ar.iihorities and other bodies in the prescribed manner; and
v. perform sdch other duties as may be prescribed.(4) The Board of Governors may, on the advice of the vice chancellcr, terminate theappointment of the Registrar on grounds of inefficiency or misconduct in accordance withprescribed procedure.\19. Treasurer, - (1) There shall be a Treasurer of the university to be appointed by theBoard of Govemors on the recommendation of the Selection Board,on such terms andconditions as may be Prescribed.(2) The experience and the professional and academic qualifications necessary forappointment to the ptjst ofthe Treasurer shall be as may be prescribed'\(3) The Treasurer shall be the chief financial officer of the University and shall: -i.managetheassets,liabilities'receipts,expenditures,funds,andinvestmentsofthe UniversitY;ii.preparetheannualandrevisedbudgetestimatesoftheUniversityandpresentthemtottEFinance&PlanningcommitteeandtheBoardofGovernors;
