25. Board of Governors: - (1) The general supervision and control of the affairs otthe University and itB powers to lay down policies Shall vest in the Board consisting of thefollowing: a(a) the Chancellor who shall bethe Chairperson of the Board of Governors;(b) the Vice Chancellor;(c) the Pro Vice Chancellors (s);(d) one member of the Government not below the rank of Joint Secretary fromthe cpncerned Ministry;(e) four persons from society at large, preferably two or at least one femalebein$ persons of distinction in the fields of administration, management,education,academics,law,accountancy,medicine,finearts,architecture,agriculture, science, technology, industry, and engineering such that theappointmentofthesepersonsreflectsabalanceacrossthevariousfields:(0 one person from amongst the alumni of the University;(S) two persons from the academic community of the country, other than anempfoyee of the University, at the level of Professor or Principal of acollege;(h)fourUniversityTeachers(Onefromeachtieri.e,Professor,AssociateProfessor, Assistant Professor and Lecturer);(i) Nominee of the Higher Education Commission;(j) Nominee of the Pakistan Medical & Dental Council;(k) One person nominated by the Khudadad Khan Foundation;(l) the Registrar, who shall be Secretary of the Board of Governors;,R(2) The numbers oiihe members of the Board of Governors may be increased throughStatutes subject to condition that the total membership ofthe Board of Governors does notexceed to twenty-one and the increase is balanced, to the extent possible, across thedifferent categories specified in sub- section (1).
(3)The Members of, the Board, other than ex-officio members shall hold office for threevears from the date of appointment;Provided that members, may serve on the BoG for more than two consecutive terms;
(4)The BoG shall meet at least twice in a calendar year.
(5)Service on the BoG shall be on honorary basis;Provided that ailual expenses may be reimbursed as prescribed'\(6)The office of nominated member shall become vacant if he resigns or fails to attendthree consecutive rneetings of Governing body without sufficient cause of leave of
