(2) Without prejudice to the generality of the foregoing powers, and subject to theprovisions of this Act and the Statutes, the Academic Council shall have the powersto:- aa) lay down proper standards of instructions, research, and examinations and toregulate ald promote the academic activities of the University;b) advise the Board of Governors on academic matters;c) regulate the conduct of teaching, research publications and examinations;d) approve the policies and procedures pertaining to student-related functionsincludingadmissions, expulsions, punishments, examinations, and certification;e) approve academic programs and the policies and procedures pertaining to thequality of academic programs;0 propose to the Board, schemes for the constitution and organization of faculties,Teaching Department and Board of studies;g) appoint paper setters and examiners for all examinations of the University afterreceiving panels of names from the relevant bodies;h) institute programs for the continued professional development of UniversityTeachers at all levels;i) recognizS the examinations of other universities or examining bodies asequivalent to the corresponding examinations of the University;j) regulate the award of studentships, sc+lolarships, exhibitions, medals, andprizes;k) . prepare an annual repo( on the academic performance of the University;l) regulate the conduct and discipline of students and faculty;m) make re$ulations on the recommendations of the Board of Faculties and theBoards ol Studies prescribing the courses of studies and the syllabi for allUniversity examinations in accordance with the policy of HEC/PM&DC andother regulatory bodies;n) regulate the admissions of students to the courses of studies and examinationsin the University;o) formulate proposals, for the planning and development of teaching andresearch {n the University;p) prepare qn annual report on the academic performance of the University;q) frame regulations for submission to the Board; andr) perform such functions as may be prescribed by Regulations or Statutes.
29. constitution, functions, and porveE of other Authorities: The constitution,functions, and powers of the Authorities for which no specific provision has been made inthis Act shall be suclr as may be prescribed by the Statutes, Regulations and Rules.
30. Appoinfnent & Commiftees by certain Authorities. - The Board of Govemors,the Academic Council and other Authorities may, from time to time, appoint such standing,special or advisory cbmmittees, as they may deem fit, and may nominate such personson these committees who are not members of the Authorities.
