(4) No Statute shall be valid unless approved by the Chancellor.
32. Regulations: (1) Subject to the provisions of this Act and the Statues, the AcademicCouncil may make Regulations, for all or any of the following matters,
(a) schemes & studies and research, including the duration of courses, number ofsubjects or papers for examination;(b) syllabi and courses of study and research programs leading to degrees,diplomas, or certificates;(c) methodology for selection and admission of students and determination of feesand other c_harges for admission to various courses and examinations;(d) courses of studies for degrees, diplomas, and certificates of the University;(e) the conditibns under which students shall be admitted to the courses and theexaminations of the University and shall become eligible for the award ofdegrees, diplomas, and certifi cates;(0 admission and expulsion of students to and from the University;(g) conditions under which a person may cany on independent research to entitlehim to a degree;(h) conduct dnd supervision of examinations, appointment of examiners anddeclarationof results;(i) maintenance of discipline among students;O determination of fees and other charges for admission to various courses;(k) institution of fellowships, scholarships, exhibitions, medals, prizes, and otherfinancial assistance;(l) conduct of Convocation and form of costumes;(mformation of Faculties, Teaching Department and Board of Studies; and(n) all other nBtters which by this Act or the Statutes, are to be or may be prescribedby Regulations.
(2) Regulations shall be proposed by the Academic Council and shall be submitted to theBoard, which may approve them or withhold approval or refer them back to the AcademicCouncil for reconsideration.
(3)Regulation proposed by the Academic council shall not be effective unless it receivesthe approval of the Board of Governors.
33. Amendment and repeal of Statutes and Rggulations: -The procedure for adding,amending, or repealing the Statutes and the Regulations shall be the same as thatprescribed respectively for framing or making the Statues and the Regulations.
34. Rutes: (1) The Authorities and the other bodies of the University may make Rules,consistent with this.hct, Statutes and the Regulations, to regulate any matter relating tothe affairs of the University which has not been specifically provided for by this Act orthatis not required to be regulated by Statutes or Regulations, including rules to regulate theconduct of business and the time and place of meetings and related matters.(2) Rules shall become effective upon approval of the Board.
