CHAPTERVIGENERAL PROVISIONS
35. First statutes. - Not withstanding anything to the contrary contained in this Act, thestatqtes set out in the schedule shall be deemed to be the First Statues made undersection 31 and shal-remain in force until they are amended or replaced by new statutesmade in accordancewith this Act.36. Benefits and insurance. - (1) The University shall constitute for the benefit of itsofficers, teachers and other employees' schemes, as may be prescribed, for tlreprovision of post-employment benefits as well as health and life insurance while inservice.
37. Service of thg University. - (1) All persons employed by the University inaccordance with the terms and conditions of service prescribed by Statutes shall hepersons in the serviQe of the University.3g. Removal of difficulties. - (1) lf any question arises as to interpretation of provisionof this act, it shall be placed before the chancellor whose decision thereon shall be thefinal.2) lf any difficulty afises in giving effect to the provisions of this Act, the Chancellor shallmake such order, not inconsistent with the provisions of this Act, as may appear to him tobe necessary for renibving this difliculty.(3)WherethisActmakesanyprovisionforanythingtobedonebutnoprovisionorlroiufficient provision [as been made as respects the authority of whom, or the time at which,or the manner in wnicrr, it shall be done, then it shall be done by such authority, at suchtime, or in such mafrher as the Chancellor may direct'39. Bar of Jurisdiction: - No Court shall have jurisdiction to entertain any proceedings,grant any injunctions or make any order relation to anything done in good faith or purportedto have been done or intended under this Act.
CHAPTER VIIINSTITUTE FUND
40. university Funds: (1) The University shall have a Fund to which shall be creditedall income from fees, charges, donations, trusts, bequests, endowments, contributions'grants, and all othef sources.41. Audit and Ac6ounb: - (1) The accounts of the University shall be maintained in aBank approved by the governing body.
