3. Teaching Department and Head of the Department - (1) There shall be aTeaching Department for each subject, or a group of allied subjects as may be approved,and each Teaching,Department shall be headed by a Chairperson.
(2)The Chairpersdi\ of a Department shall be appointed by the Board on therecommendation of the Vice Chancellor from amongst the senior Professors or AssociateProfessors, other than Professor already working as Dean, for a period of three years andshall be eligible for reappointment.
(3)The Chairperson of the Teaching Department shall plan, organize, and supervise thework of the Depafthent in accordance with the provisions of this Act and shall beresponsible to the Qean of lhe Faculty in which his/her Department is comprised for thework of his/her Department.
(4) The Chairperson of the Teaching Department shall under the supervision of the ViceChancellor and the Dean, exercise all administrative, financial, and academic powers andsuch other duties or powers as may be delegated to him/her.
(s)The Chairpersoe of the Department shall prepare a comprehensive and annual report'1on the performance of the Department at undergraduate and post-graduate levels andfaculty research and development and submil the same to the Dean of the faculty forevaluation.
4. Board of Studies. - (1) There shall be a Board of Studies for each subject or groupof subjects as may be prescribed by the Regulations.',\'
(2) Each Board of Studies shall consist of:
a)
b)
c)
d)
the Chairperson of the Teaching Department concerned;all Professors and Associate Professors in the Teaching Departmentconcerned;such Uniiersity Teachers, other than Professors or Associate Professors, to beappointett by the Academic Council; andthree experts, otherthan the Teachers of the University, to be appointed by theVice Chancellor.
